      "metadata": {
        "split_group": "direct_furnisher_exception"
      },
      "narrative": "The consumer sent the bank a direct dispute at the bank's published dispute address, but the dispute concerned only a courthouse judgment appearing as public-record information and did not challenge account or relationship information furnished by the bank. The CRA side separately had a valid direct dispute about a furnished auto-loan item, notified the furnisher timely, completed a reasonable reinvestigation in 24 days, verified that auto-loan item, recorded current status, and sent a timely results notice. No reseller, reinsertion, or consumer-statement branch applies.\n",
      "provenance": "authored",
      "structured_fields": {},
      "title": "Direct furnisher dispute concerns only public-record judgment"
